WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.509 --> 00:00:11.900
Many of you probably think all the countries
in the Arabian peninsula are insanely wealthy�

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:12.900
Right!?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.270
I mean this is the region where Qatar, Dubai,
and the rest of the oil rich monarchies are�

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.070
Nonetheless, right in this region of the planet
is a country that is extremely poor.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:25.900
A place with a GDP per capita lower than that
of Tanzania or Senegal...

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.810
The name of this country is YEMEN and currently
it is going through a civil war that has lasted

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:37.100
for two years.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.579
And look, this is no small war... In fact,
the War in Yemen is the Arabian equivalent

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:43.050
to the War in Vietnam.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:47.499
Here we find two of the biggest powers in
the Muslim world supporting different sides

00:00:47.499 --> 00:00:48.659
of the conflict.

00:00:48.659 --> 00:00:53.170
On the one hand, we have the Yemeni government,
supported by Saudi Arabia and all their allies,

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.969
including United States.

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:59.340
And on the other side, there is the revolutionaries,
backed by Iran.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:06.310
And between these two sides, there is the
Yemeni branch of DAESH, the so-called ANSAR-AL-SHARIA

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.260
movement.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:12.730
If you've been subscribed to VisualPolitik
for a while, you already know that Saudi Arabia

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.820
has the third best equipped army in the entire
world.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.830
Plus, they have the support of American drones
and the armies of neighbouring countries.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:26.150
They have more than 180 state of the art combat
jets and 300,000 soldiers armed with the best

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.150
weapons.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.670
On the other side, they have less than half
the number of soldiers, and the weapons they

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:35.890
are armed with are far from modern...

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.960
It seems like a pretty unequal fight, right?!

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:47.700
Well, in that case, it might suprise you to
learn that Saudi Arabia is losing this war...

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.610
Saudi Arabia says prepared for ceasefire in
Yemen if Houthis agree.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.790
And now you might wonder... How exactly is
this possible?!

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:59.120
How is it possible to explain why one of the
most advanced armies in the world can't

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.690
beat a bunch of guerillas?

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:03.070
Well, today we are going to answer this question.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:07.890
But before we get into any of that, let's
have a look at the history...

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:12.640
WHO IS WHO IN YEMEN

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.400
The first thing we need to understand is that
this is not the first time Yemen has had a

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.400
civil war.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.970
In fact, this is the third one in just 25
years.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:25.650
Yemen is a country divided by both ideology
and religion.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:34.680
Indeed, before the 1990s, Yemen was split
into two different countries.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:40.739
We had South Yemen, with a communist government,
and then there was North Yemen who had a pro-Saudi

00:02:40.739 --> 00:02:41.739
government.

00:02:41.739 --> 00:02:42.739
In 1990, these two halves merged into modern
day Yemen.

00:02:42.739 --> 00:02:45.879
And the guy you are seeing on the screen now,
ALI ABDULLAH SALEH, who was the president

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:55.530
of the north, started ruling over the entire
country from its capital: the city of SANA'A.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:03:00.060
As you can imagine, Saleh is one of those
politicians who considers democracy and human

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.330
rights as pretty 'optional'.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:08.200
Four years into this new countries history,
and former southern communist leaders started

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.639
an uprising against Saleh's government.

00:03:10.639 --> 00:03:15.099
This war only lasted a few months, and the
new government won with the assistance of

00:03:15.099 --> 00:03:16.120
the Saudi's.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:21.209
A decade later, in 2004, Yemen had further
anti-government turmoil, this time, the opposition

00:03:21.209 --> 00:03:23.950
was a rebel group of Shia muslims.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:29.389
Remember their name because there are important
for today's war: they are the HOUTHI REBELS.

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:32.019
Again, the Saleh government beat down this
uprising.

00:03:32.019 --> 00:03:35.999
But hold on a minute because we're not done
yet...

00:03:35.999 --> 00:03:41.359
In 2011, with the Arab spring in full-swing,
the citizens rebelled against Saleh... again.

00:03:41.359 --> 00:03:45.799
But this time, Saleh left power with his prime
minister, MANSUR AL-HADI.

00:03:45.799 --> 00:03:49.040
This new president found himself in the control
of a terribly weak government.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.409
Further, Al Qaeda was destroying the country.

00:03:52.409 --> 00:03:56.029
And the protestors, well they kept protesting...

00:03:56.029 --> 00:03:57.889
Now, remember those Houthi rebels?

00:03:57.889 --> 00:04:04.060
Well, they came back, but this time they were
far more powerful and had a lot of support.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:10.010
And this explains why in 2014, they took over
the government...

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:14.980
Alright, so now you might be wondering...
What did AL HADI do?

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.400
Well, he left the capital and moved to the
city of ADEN, in the South of the country,

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:23.870
to start a provisional government.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:30.100
Now, remember here, that Saudi Arabia is a
SUNNI muslim country.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.760
And who is the biggest enemy of Sunni muslims?

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.590
Well, yep, that would be the SHIA muslims...

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:39.150
These are exactly the people who have conquered
the capital of Yemen.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:43.370
And THIS explains why the Saudi's are so
keen on supporting Al Hadi and his provisional

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.840
government in ADEN.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:50.210
The finally we also have DAESH, AKA Islamic
State, in the mix as well (who are an enemy

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:51.370
of both sides).

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:53.492
Alright, so now we have, the Houthi rebels
and their supporters.

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:58.590
The Houthis are Shia muslims, and therefore,
they are friends with Iran.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:02.630
On the other hand, AL HADI is in ADEN and
he is supported by the Saudi's...

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:07.870
And the Saudi's will do whatever it takes
to ensure that Iranian influence in Yemen

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.200
is minimised.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:14.560
You probably remember from one of our previous
videos that Saudi Arabia and Iran are die-hard

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:15.560
enemies.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:27.340
And thus, in 2015, a new Yemeni civil war
started...

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:33.130
A NATURAL FORTRESS

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:39.210
When we think about Saudi Arabia, we think
of a big desert with clean sand and dunes.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.240
Yemen is different.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:45.290
It is a country full of mountains almost as
high as the Rockies in the US.

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:50.750
Some peaks are higher than 3600 meters.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:57.040
All of this makes it really hard to transport
a big army, no matter how well equipped it

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.040
is.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:02.000
For instance, the Saudis utilize a tank model
called the M1A1 ABRAMS.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.800
This is like the BMW of tanks.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:10.510
Now imagine a convoy of these machines crossing
a path where they have to in single file...

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:16.520
All you would need is just a couple of guerrilla
warriors, with say an RPG 7 rocket launcher

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:19.120
and you could destroy the entire battalion.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:24.090
The RPG 7 is that rocket launcher you can
see on videogames like Call of Duty and it

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.800
has a market price of around $3000.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:35.450
The M1A1 ABRAMS on the other hand, costs around
$6 million.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.880
But not only that!

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:44.670
As we said at the start of this video, the
Saudi coalition has over 180 combat jets and

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.270
also American drones.

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:48.860
But there is a further problem...

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:53.930
In a landscape full of mountains and caves
it is really easy to hide from these drones.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:07:00.020
Not even the state of the art radars can see,
in detail, what's inside the caves.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:08.680
And, of course, the Houthi warriors know the
battlefield like the back of their hands and

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.890
they know where all the good hiding places
are.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:15.640
In many cases, they can go from one village
to another without being exposed to the drone

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:16.640
radars.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.700
They can also hide their weapons inside the
caves.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:23.780
But that's not all... Even though these
guerrillas have no Hummers or other modern

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:27.380
vehicle, they have something better... ANIMALS!

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.460
Yep, you heard that right.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:35.490
In those high mountain areas, the most effective
way to transport something is by using donkeys

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.170
or camels.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:43.360
So, in other words, the only way of tracking
the movements of these guerrilla warriors

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:46.080
is by having people behind their lines.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:51.200
Now we're not exactly talking about 007-like
spies here, but rather local citizens who

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.820
are willing to help or soldiers who are close
to enemy lines.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:59.230
Alright, so even with these problems, you
might still be wondering how the Saudi's

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:00.380
are getting beat.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:03.940
The scales still seemed to be tipped pretty
far in their favour...

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:13.530
A DEMOTIVATED ARMY?

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:17.330
Many of you might think that the political
system of a country has nothing to do with

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.010
the way they organize their army and conduct
war...

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:21.470
Right?

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:26.680
Well, actually in a country like Saudi Arabia,
they are REALLY connected.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:31.020
In an absolute monarchy, like they have in
Saudi Arabia, the royal house cannot trust

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:32.020
their army.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:37.649
Their main obsession is keeping control over
the entire military from the top to the bottom.

00:08:37.649 --> 00:08:46.010
This is why the decision making is slower
than in any other army...

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:53.530
Let's look at a hypothetical example...
Imagine a soldier who discovers a machine

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:55.460
gun nest 300 meters out.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:09:00.960
In a western army like the American or British,
that soldier can easily ask for reinforcement

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:01.960
by radio.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:06.450
Usually, that information would be passed
onto the Air Force, who would give the exact

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:07.900
coordinates to a pilot nearby.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:11.580
In a matter of minutes, a combat jet is bombing
the machine gun nest.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.070
But... What happens in the the Saudi army?

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.910
Well... that very same soldier would have
to report to a sergeant, then that sergeant

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.130
talks to the higher officers and, finally,
by the time the decision has worked it's

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:24.270
way up to someone who can actually make it...
it's been longer than an hour.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:28.910
The 60 minutes here are the difference between
neutralizing an enemy position... or losing

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:30.550
a soldier.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:36.410
And... the same goes for military training.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:41.440
Most Saudi officials come from the Royal Houses
and they didn't go through any academic

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:45.870
military training.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:51.080
They got their position due to pure nepotism
and this means a distinct lack of knowledge

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:52.080
and skills.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.990
The same goes with for normal soldiers as
well.

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:58.860
As you know, in these oil monarchies, most
of the native citizens work as civil servants,

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.210
with sky high salaries.

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:04.330
They don't know anything about discipline
and hard work...

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.160
Let's look at an example.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:16.940
In the video here, you can see how they cannot
even protect a tank with infantry.

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:22.930
Don't forget that inside the tank it is
hard to see and hear the outside.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:27.740
This is why, a basic principle of war is that
you always want to have soldiers walking around

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.980
the tank so they can see if someone is firing.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.310
This really is War 101.

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:38.250
Nonetheless, the Saudi's missed War 101,
and this explains why it is so easy to destroy

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:45.470
their tanks with such cheap weaponry...

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:46.870
Just have a look at this other video.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:54.630
Here you can see how someone get's close
enough to a tank to put a bomb on it!

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:59.570
On the other hand, surprisingly, the Houthi
rebels have a more western management system.

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:05.100
Small groups can react quickly and they don't
need to go all the way up through the hierarchy.

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:12.730
Plus, their motivation is way higher because
they just cannot retire.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:16.090
Arguably, they are defending their home from
a foreign army.

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:21.010
In summary, the war in Yemen is an excellent
example of how strategy is more important

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:28.170
than weaponry, and that an authoritarian system
makes for less efficient armies.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:33.270
Sadly, the fact that the Saudi's are losing
this war doesn't mean they are not killing

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:34.270
people.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:37.050
In fact, the opposite is true...

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:40.250
Death toll in Yemen conflict passes 10,000

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:44.310
Unfortunately, what could have been solved
in a peaceful, democratic, way, has become

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:48.720
a war of attrition that will leave a footprint
on this country for generations to come.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:52.750
And now the question is... Do you think Saudi's
can turn the table on this conflict?

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:56.200
Or are we going to see this conflict last
for a long time to come?

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.620
Please let us know your thoughts in the comments
below.

